    "description": "Original MCQs for a workplace-compliance training module on the revised Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (revidiertes Datenschutzgesetz, revDSG/nDSG, SR 235.1, in force 1 September 2023) and its implementing Data Protection Ordinance (Datenschutzverordnung, DSV, SR 235.11). Five topics: scope and key concepts (Art. 1-5, 14 DSG); processing principles and grounds of justification (Art. 6, 7, 30, 31, 34 DSG); rights of the data subject (Art. 21, 25-29, 32 DSG, Art. 16-22 DSV); duties of controllers and processors (Art. 8-12, 22-24 DSG, Art. 1-7, 14, 15, 24, 25 DSV); and disclosure abroad, supervision and criminal provisions (Art. 16, 17, 49-51, 60-66 DSG, Art. 8-12 and Annex 1 DSV). Content is independently phrased and grounded directly in the Fedlex text of the DSG (Stand 1.9.2023) and the DSV (Stand 15.9.2024), NOT sourced or paraphrased from any commercial compliance-training or e-learning vendor's material. Deliberately covers the points where Swiss law departs from the GDPR, since those are where GDPR-trained learners are most likely to be wrong. See-also: this is a SEPARATE module from 'datenschutz' (EU GDPR / German BDSG) - the two regimes are related but legally distinct and are cross-linked, not merged (PO decision 2026-08-16).",
